  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Health for Rural Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Digital Health for Rural Youth&quot; project bridges the gap in access to health information on GBV, sexual and reproductive health, and mental well-being for marginalized rural youth in Uganda. Using Mobimocc, an IVR platform that works on feature phones, requires no internet, and is free for users, the project provides accessible, stigma-free health education. Youth will learn about their rights, health choices, and available services, with special focus on young women. Collaborating with local leaders, schools, and youth groups, we aim to enhance community engagement and platform adoption. Digital literacy training will ensure effective navigation of the platform. A continuous feedback loop will adapt the platform to users&#x2019; needs, empowering youth with the tools to improve their health and well-being.

The &quot;Digital Health for Rural Youth&quot; project aims to provide rural youth in Uganda, especially young women, with access to critical health information on GBV, sexual and reproductive health, and mental well-being through mobile platforms like Mobimocc. The project will enhance digital literacy and empower youth to make informed health decisions.

Objectives:
Deliver accurate health information through mobile technology.
Improve digital literacy among rural youth.
Empower youth, especially women, to take control of their health.

Outcomes:
Improved health awareness and decision-making.
Increased access to support services.
Reduced stigma around sensitive health topics.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Woman Uganda Limited</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Woman Uganda is a non-profit organization focused on empowering women and youth in Uganda, particularly those in rural areas, through digital literacy, entrepreneurship, and access to technology-driven solutions. The organization strives to bridge the digital divide, improve access to information, and promote gender equality through the use of technology.

Vision: To create an inclusive society where women and youth, especially in rural areas, are empowered through technology, leading to improved livelihoods, gender equality, and enhanced access to information and opportunities.

Mission: To equip women and youth with the necessary digital skills, promote their rights, and use technology as a tool for economic empowerment and social change, with a focus on rural and marginalized communities.

Objectives:
1. Promote digital literacy and entrepreneurship among women and youth.
Empower women and marginalized youth through access to digital tools and resources.
2. Advocate for digital inclusion, gender equality, and women&#x2019;s rights in Uganda.
3. Address key issues like gender-based violence (GBV), health, and education through technology-based solutions.

Values:
1.Inclusivity: Ensuring all women and youth, regardless of background or ability, have access to opportunities.
2. Empowerment: Supporting individuals to take charge of their futures through technology.
3. Integrity: Operating transparently, ethically, and responsibly in all projects.
4. Innovation: Embracing new technologiesand solutions to address societal challenges.
5. Collaboration: Partnering with other organizations, governments, and stakeholders to achieve sustainable impact.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
